ANN-0145,Q10,Explain Graph Neural Networks,CAND-72c1c3f90ecf,papers/Real-time network security: Integrating ANN and dynamic graph-based.pdf,2,,"Our proposed D-MAGIC (Dynamic Model for cybersecurity At- tack detection using GNNs Into Clustering) and SAGA (Sophisticated Anomaly detection with GNN into ANN) models enhance detection ca- pabilities by incorporating graph-based learning. Both models leverage Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) to generate node embeddings, captur- ing complex relationships between network entities, which traditional vector-based approaches often overlook [10]. By utilizing zero-shot learning, these models can detect previously unseen attacks without re- quiring labeled examples, allowing them to generalize beyond known threats. Additionally, they analyze network traﬃc on a packet-by-packet basis, enabling real-time detection and immediate response to potential threats as they emerge.",,,,,,
