ANN-0171,Q12,Explain Positional Encoding in Transformers,CAND-387090c30016,papers/Vaswani2017_Attention_Is_All_You_Need.pdf,2,,"Most competitive neural sequence transduction models have an encoder-decoder structure [5, 2, 35]. Here, the encoder maps an input sequence of symbol representations (x1, ..., xn) to a sequence of continuous representations z = (z1, ..., zn). Given z, the decoder then generates an output sequence (y1, ..., ym) of symbols one element at a time. At each step the model is auto-regressive [10], consuming the previously generated symbols as additional input when generating the next.
