ANN-0385,Q26,How does LoRA adapt Transformer weight matrices?,CAND-cc62304dbcf2,papers/Hu2021_LoRA.pdf,10,7 UNDERSTANDING THE LOW-RANK UPDATES,"Given a limited parameter budget, which types of weights should we adapt with LoRA to obtain the best performance on downstream tasks? As mentioned in Section 4.2, we only consider weight matrices in the self-attention module. We set a parameter budget of 18M (roughly 35MB if stored in FP16) on GPT-3 175B, which corresponds to r = 8 if we adapt one type of attention weights or r = 4 if we adapt two types, for all 96 layers. The result is presented in Table 5.
