ANN-0552,Q38,How does tiling reduce HBM memory traffic in FlashAttention?,CAND-678ab86bc11e,upload_cb7badb2,4,4. Theoretical IO Complexity and Memory Efficiency,"Standard attention requires O(N^2) HBM accesses because it reads and writes intermediate matrices S and P of size N x N. FlashAttention requires only O(N^2 d^2 / M) HBM accesses, where d is head dimension and M is the size of SRAM.
When M is proportional to d, the IO complexity scales linearly as O(N) relative to the sequence length. This reduction in memory bandwidth pressure converts memory-boun",,,,,,
