For large-scale data implementations, a queue-based mechanism can be introduced to manage client nodes dynamically. By maintaining a queue for active client nodes and removing inactive ones based on a predeﬁned timeout or data volume threshold, the system prevents exces- sive memory consumption while ensuring eﬃcient real-time detection. This adaptive approach allows the model to scale eﬃciently without overwhelming system resources.
Additionally, Knowledge Distillation on Graphs (KDG) can be em- ployed to distill essential structural and feature information from larger models into a more compact representation, reducing computational overhead while maintaining detection performance. This adaptive ap- proach allows the model to scale eﬃciently without overwhelming sys- tem resources.For further information, see [41].
