ANN-0642,Q44,Explain the Ricardian theory of comparative advantage.,CAND-c3fe4ed9326d,papers/Real-time network security: Integrating ANN and dynamic graph-based.pdf,10,Table 3 Data Distribution for CSE-CIC-IDS-2018 dataset.,"• Graph Attention Network (GAT) as a GNN Baseline: To strengthen the fairness and depth of our comparative analysis, and to evaluate the contribution of the GNN component (Step 3) in isolation, we ad- ditionally include a GNN-based baseline utilizing a GAT. In this vari- ant, the original GCN used in D-MAGIC is replaced with a GAT archi- tecture. GATs extend conventional GCNs by incorporating an atten- tion mechanism that adaptively assigns importance weights to neigh- boring nodes during message aggregation. This enables the model to capture more nuanced structural dependencies within the graph. By comparing D-MAGIC (GCN-based) with its GAT-based counterpart, we assess whether employing a more expressive GNN architecture yields measurable performance improvements in our anomaly de- tection framework.",,,,,,
